Please address the comments from this code review:

## Overall Comments
- In `fetchWithTimeout`, the internally created `AbortController` fully replaces any caller-provided `signal`, which means upstream cancellation (e.g. user-initiated abort) can’t be honored; consider wiring an optional existing `signal` into the controller so either the caller or the timeout can cancel the request.
- The `Retry-After` handling in `fetchWithRetry` assumes a numeric delta-seconds value and ignores HTTP-date format or fractional seconds; if you expect diverse upstreams, you may want to parse both formats and handle non-integer values more defensively rather than relying on `parseInt`.

## Individual Comments

### Comment 1
